          "short": "Reflect in the $x$-axis, then translate 3 units right and 1 unit up.",
          "worked": "Reflecting in the $x$-axis gives $y=-x^2$. Translating 3 units right gives $y=-(x-3)^2$. Translating 1 unit up gives $y=1-(x-3)^2$. The vertex is $(3,1)$ and the arms open downwards.",
